--- KEY LESSON (worth a memory / handler note) ---
In Vitis HLS, `#pragma HLS PIPELINE` on an OUTER loop force-unrolls ALL inner
loops to fit the pipeline. To pipeline a long reduction WITHOUT exploding DSPs,
put the PIPELINE pragma on the REDUCTION loop itself (chunked by a modest
UNROLL factor), not on the loop above it. v2/v3 had it on the j-loop → full
k-unroll → 1500+ DSP. v4 moved it to the k-loop → 36 DSP.

--- T0029 readiness ---
T0029 stacks 12 of this layer. Per orch directive: time-multiplex ONE physical
v4 instance 12×, do NOT inline 12 copies. With v4 at 36 DSP / 72 URAM,
time-multiplexed T0029 stays ≈ 36 DSP / ~72-100 URAM (one instance + 12 weight
sets in BRAM). Inlining 12× would be 432 DSP / 864 URAM (URAM over again).
T0029 is now unblocked and feasible.
